// Runtime/ServiceBehaviour.maxon — `<T>.__behave` and `<T>.__finish`, the two functions the
// compiler synthesizes for every SERVICE: `__behave(cown, request)` runs one message and
// `__finish(cown)` drops the state. The cown's runner (`CownRuntime.__cown_run`) calls them through
// the cown's `CownOffBehave` and `CownOffFinish` words.
// Specified in `specs/services.md` §"What the compiler synthesizes".
//
// ⭐⭐ **THEY ARE BUILT AT THE MAXON TIER, ON `ModuleInit.SynthesizedFunction`, AND THE TIER IS THE WHOLE
// WIRING.** `__behave` CALLS USER CODE — one handler per message, with the receiver, the argument slotting,
// the ranged-alias widths and the dual-register error ABI a real call has — so building it as already-lowered
// `StdOp`s would be a second copy of `lowerCall`, which is the duplication this compiler pays for hardest.
// Appended to the merged module beside `__module_init`, they are ordinary program code to everything below:
// `SemanticCheck` type-checks their calls, `scanRuntimeUsage` sees their `__cown_unknown_tag` /
// `__mm_decref` / `__destruct_<T>` calls and installs the floor they need, and `lowerMaxonToStd` lowers them
// like anything else.
//
// ⭐ **ONE CONSEQUENCE WORTH STATING, BECAUSE IT DELETES A WHOLE OBLIGATION.** `AsyncReleaser` has
// to DECLARE what its bodies will call (`declareAsyncReleaserNeeds`) because they are Std-tier
// bodies built AFTER the runtime-needs scan — rule 2 of `RuntimeUsage`'s header. These functions are built
// BEFORE that scan, so every drop they emit is DISCOVERED: each payload's drop and the state's are
// rooted by the ordinary walk.
//
// ⛔⛔⛔ **EVERY TYPE THIS FILE RESOLVES OUT OF THE SIGNATURE INDEX STAYS IN THE INDEX'S NAME SPACE, AND
// `SynthesizedFunction.mint` IS WHAT CROSSES IT.** *"Names travel between interners; ids never
// do"* — an id is a number, and it means whatever name sits at that number in the table you read it against.
// The carrier's `projectScopedNameId` crosses every id a MINT is given, so a caller that hands it one which
// is ALREADY project-scoped gets a SECOND crossing, from the wrong side: the number is resolved through the
// index, lands on an unrelated name, and that name is re-interned into the project.
//
// ⛔ Payload types resolved `into: project.typeNames` and then minted are crossed twice. On a program with two
// services where one message takes a `String` its handler calls a method on and another takes a
// `Logger.handle`, the tables diverge by one entry and `__behave`'s handle argument comes out as
// `E3005 argument type mismatch for 'sink': expected 'Logger.handle', got 'ExitCode'` — a refusal of a
// correct program with no file or line, because the check walks THIS synthesized body. The same misread id
// also chooses `classifyUnionPayload`'s class and `managedFieldDropCallee`'s callee, which is a payload
// dropped through the wrong destructor or not at all. A small program does not show it: the two tables agree
// at every id until enough types are declared to push them apart.
//
// ⇒ **`signatures.indexTypeNames()` at every one of those doors, and `project.typeNames` at exactly two:**
// `stateType`, which is interned by NAME rather than read out of the index and is handed to
// `SynthesizedFunction.open` (which stores parameter ids RAW — see the carrier), and the drop callee that
// pairs with it. A `typeNames:` argument and the `MaxonType` beside it must always be one table.
//
// ⭐⭐ **NO `__do_<m>` TRAMPOLINES, BECAUSE A DISPATCH ARM HERE IS NOT A `match` ARM.** **E2049**'s
// one statement per arm is a SOURCE rule (`Parser.parseArmBody`, `statementFormRole`)
// and `__behave` is not source: at the IR tier a `switch` arm is a BLOCK, which holds as many ops as
// it likes. So there is ONE function per service and the handler call and the drops all live in the
// arm — which is also what makes the un-consumed-payload drop expressible at all.

// ⭐⭐ **BUILD `<T>.__behave` AND `<T>.__finish` FOR EVERY SERVICE IN THE PROGRAM.** Called from
// `Compiler.lowerTheProgram` directly after `installManagedGlobalInit`, at the same tier and for
// the same reason — see this file's header, and `ModuleInit`'s, which states the position's whole
// argument.
//
// A program that spawns nothing builds NOTHING here: `serviceTypeRoster` is empty, which is every program
// that never writes `spawn`.
export function installServiceBehaviours(module MaxonModule, project Project, signatures ProgramSignatures) throws CompileError
	let discovered = serviceTypeRoster(signatures)

	if discovered.count() == 0 'spawnsNothing'
		return
	end 'spawnsNothing'

	let services = servicesInDeclarationOrder(discovered, signatures: signatures, fileRanks: project.emissionRanks)

	let funcNames = try FunctionNameIndex.create(module.functions, project: project)

	// ⭐ **ONE WALK OF THE MODULE FOR EVERY SERVICE, NOT ONE PER SERVICE.** The walk is Θ(program), so
	// driving it from inside the roster loop would multiply the whole module by the number of service types
	// — the one place in this file where a per-type constant would become a per-type PASS.
	let spawned = spawnedInstancesByService(module, services: services)

	for i in 0 upto services.count() 'eachService'
		let typeName = try services.get(i) otherwise panic("installServiceBehaviours: services.get OOB at {i} on a list walked to its own count")

		if project.poison.declaresANominalType(typeName) 'declaredInAFailedFile'
			continue
		end 'declaredInAFailedFile'

		if project.poison.holdsAnAbandonedBodyOf(typeName, declaredIn: spawnTargetLayoutOf(signatures, typeName: typeName).declFilePath) 'aHandlerWasAbandoned'
			continue
		end 'aHandlerWasAbandoned'

		buildServiceBehaviours(module, project: project, signatures: signatures, funcNames: funcNames, typeName: typeName, instances: try spawned.get(i) otherwise panic("installServiceBehaviours: spawned.get OOB at {i} — one bucket is pushed per service before the walk"))
	end 'eachService'
end 'installServiceBehaviours'

function servicesInDeclarationOrder(discovered NameRoster, signatures ProgramSignatures, fileRanks FileEmissionRankMap) returns NameRoster
	let positions = DeclarationPositionArray.create(discovered.count(), zeroed: false)

	for typeName in discovered 'eachService'
		let layout = spawnTargetLayoutOf(signatures, typeName: typeName)
		positions.push(DeclarationPosition.of(fileRanks, path: layout.declFilePath, line: layout.declLine, column: layout.declColumn, kind: "the service type", name: typeName))
	end 'eachService'

	let ordered = NameRoster.create(discovered.count(), zeroed: false)

	for slot in declarationsInPositionOrder(positions) 'eachInDeclarationOrder'
		ordered.push(try discovered.get(slot) otherwise panic("servicesInDeclarationOrder: discovered.get OOB at {slot}"))
	end 'eachInDeclarationOrder'

	return ordered
end 'servicesInDeclarationOrder'

// ⭐⭐ **THE BEHAVIOURS ARE MONOMORPHIC WHERE THE COMPANIONS ARE NOT, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE OF WHAT A GENERIC
// SERVICE COSTS.** One `<T>.request` and one `<T>.handle` serve every instantiation — neither carries a type
// argument — but `__behave` CALLS the handlers and `__finish` DROPS the state, and both of those are per-instance facts:
// a `returns T` handler takes the instance's layout descriptor, and the state releases through
// `__destruct_<mangled>`. A shared body has nothing to source either from (a synthesized function carries no
// dictionary of its own), so there is one pair per instantiation the program spawns.
function buildServiceBehaviours(module MaxonModule, project Project, signatures ProgramSignatures, funcNames FunctionNameIndex, typeName ByteArray, instances GenericInstanceIdArray)
	if not signatures.structDeclaresTypeParams(typeName) 'monomorphic'
		buildServiceBehaviourPair(module, project: project, signatures: signatures, funcNames: funcNames, typeName: typeName, instance: ServiceStateInstance.monomorphic)
		return
	end 'monomorphic'

	// ⛔⛔ **AN EMPTY BUCKET BUILDS NOTHING AND IS NOT AN ASSERTION FAILURE**. The ROSTER is
	// built from the discovery walk's raw token candidates, so a type can be on it with not one
	// `serviceSpawn` op behind it. There is nothing to build behaviours for and nothing that could call
	// one.
	let mangledInstances = NameRoster.create(instances.count(), zeroed: false)
	let instanceOrder = DeclarationOrder.create(instances.count(), zeroed: false)

	for gid in instances 'eachMangled'
		instanceOrder.push(mangledInstances.count())
		mangledInstances.push(signatures.mangleGenericInstance(gid))
	end 'eachMangled'

	instanceOrder.sortBy(function(left ElementIndex, right ElementIndex) gives compareBytesOrdinally(try mangledInstances.get(left) otherwise panic("buildServiceBehaviours: mangledInstances.get OOB at {left}"), right: try mangledInstances.get(right) otherwise panic("buildServiceBehaviours: mangledInstances.get OOB at {right}")))

	for slot in instanceOrder 'eachInstantiation'
		buildServiceBehaviourPair(module, project: project, signatures: signatures, funcNames: funcNames, typeName: typeName, instance: ServiceStateInstance.at(try instances.get(slot) otherwise panic("buildServiceBehaviours: instances.get OOB at {slot}")))
	end 'eachInstantiation'
end 'buildServiceBehaviours'

// One bucket of spawned instantiations per entry of `services`, in that order.
typealias SpawnedInstanceBuckets = Array with GenericInstanceIdArray

// Which instantiations the walk has already bucketed. A gid determines its own base, so one set serves
// every service and no gid can land in two buckets.
typealias SpawnedInstanceSet = Set with GenericInstanceId

// ⭐⭐ **EVERY INSTANTIATION THIS PROGRAM ACTUALLY SPAWNS, READ OFF THE OPS, IN ONE WALK.** The index knows
// every instance the program NAMES, which is a larger set — an instance nothing spawns would get a pair
// whose handler calls and state drop nothing ever reaches, and whose reply the `spawn` road never judged
// (`ServiceCompanions.uncarriableReplyResultNoun` refuses a reply the cell cannot carry, and it is asked at
// the `spawn`). The `serviceSpawn` ops are the exact set, and their state values are read through the same
// classifier `LowerMaxonToStd.spawnedStateInstance` uses, so the pair that is BUILT is the pair that is
// CALLED.
//
// ⚠ **THE ROSTER LOOKUP INSIDE THE WALK IS OVER DISTINCT SERVICE TYPES**, which is a count an author writes
// by hand (`serviceTypeRoster`'s own bound) — unlike the INSTANTIATIONS, which grow with the program and are
// therefore deduped through a set rather than a scan.
function spawnedInstancesByService(module MaxonModule, services NameRoster) returns SpawnedInstanceBuckets
	let buckets = SpawnedInstanceBuckets.create(services.count(), zeroed: false)

	for _ in services 'eachService'
		buckets.push(GenericInstanceIdArray.create(0))
	end 'eachService'

	let seen = SpawnedInstanceSet.create()

	for func in module.functions 'eachFunc'
		for blockRef in func.blockRefs 'eachBlock'
			let block = try module.blocks.get(blockRef) otherwise panic("spawnedInstancesByService: blockRef from func.blockRefs not in module.blocks")

			for opIdx in block.bodyOps() 'eachOp'
				noteSpawnedInstance(try module.ops.get(opIdx) otherwise panic("spawnedInstancesByService: opIdx {opIdx} not in module.ops"), func: func, services: services, buckets: buckets, seen: seen)
			end 'eachOp'
		end 'eachBlock'
	end 'eachFunc'

	return buckets
end 'spawnedInstancesByService'

function noteSpawnedInstance(op MaxonOp, func IrFunction, services NameRoster, buckets SpawnedInstanceBuckets, seen SpawnedInstanceSet)
	if not maxonOpIsServiceSpawn(op) 'startsNoService'
		return
	end 'startsNoService'

	match op 'op'
		serviceSpawn(_, spawnedType, state, _, _, _, _, _, _, _, _) then bucketSpawnedInstance(func, spawnedType: spawnedType, state: state, services: services, buckets: buckets, seen: seen)
		default panic("noteSpawnedInstance: `maxonOpIsServiceSpawn` answered true for an op that is not a `serviceSpawn`")
	end 'op'
end 'noteSpawnedInstance'

// One `serviceSpawn`'s instantiation, into its service's bucket. A state standing at NO instantiation is a
// monomorphic service's plain box and is bucketed by nobody — `buildServiceBehaviours` is where that is judged.
function bucketSpawnedInstance(func IrFunction, spawnedType ByteArray, state ValueId, services NameRoster, buckets SpawnedInstanceBuckets, seen SpawnedInstanceSet)
	let tag = try func.valueTags.get(state) otherwise panic("bucketSpawnedInstance: v{state} is not in '{String.from(func.name)}'s dense value-tag column")
	let nameId = try func.valueNameIds.get(state) otherwise panic("bucketSpawnedInstance: v{state} is not in '{String.from(func.name)}'s dense value-name column")

	match serviceStateInstanceOfValueType(tag, nameId: nameId) 'stands'
		monomorphic then return
		at(gid) then noteDistinctInstance(gid, spawnedType: spawnedType, services: services, buckets: buckets, seen: seen)
	end 'stands'
end 'bucketSpawnedInstance'

function noteDistinctInstance(gid GenericInstanceId, spawnedType ByteArray, services NameRoster, buckets SpawnedInstanceBuckets, seen SpawnedInstanceSet)
	if seen.contains(gid) 'alreadyBucketed'
		return
	end 'alreadyBucketed'

	for i in 0 upto services.count() 'eachService'
		let listed = try services.get(i) otherwise panic("noteDistinctInstance: services.get OOB at {i} on a list walked to its own count")

		if not listed.equals(spawnedType) 'anotherService'
			continue
		end 'anotherService'

		let bucket = try buckets.get(i) otherwise panic("noteDistinctInstance: buckets.get OOB at {i} — one bucket is pushed per service before the walk")
		seen.insert(gid)
		bucket.push(gid)
		return
	end 'eachService'

	// ⭐⭐ **FALLING OUT IS THE ANSWER FOR A SPAWN OF A TYPE THE ROSTER DOES NOT CARRY, AND IT IS NOT THE
	// LINK FAILURE OF A TYPE ON ONE OF THE TWO LISTS.** That failure is a handle whose behaviours nothing
	// built. This is the other direction — an op whose type the roster declined —
	// and the roster declines exactly the targets `Parser.parseSpawn` refuses at the source
	// (`serviceTypeRoster` skips every verdict but `startsAService`). A program holding such an op is one
	// the parse has already rejected, so building nothing for it is what leaves the author with their own
	// diagnostic instead of a second finding about its wreckage.
end 'noteDistinctInstance'

// The two functions' parameters, by the ValueId the parameter numbering reserves for each — `ModuleInit`'s
// `ExitCodeParam` shape, and for its reason: a synthesized function has no parameter NAMES, so argument `n`
// is a named constant or it is a bare number at every use.
let ServiceCownParam = 0 as ValueId
let ServiceRequestParam = 1 as ValueId

function buildServiceBehaviourPair(module MaxonModule, project Project, signatures ProgramSignatures, funcNames FunctionNameIndex, typeName ByteArray, instance ServiceStateInstance)
	buildServiceBehave(module, project: project, signatures: signatures, funcNames: funcNames, typeName: typeName, instance: instance)
	buildServiceFinish(module, project: project, signatures: signatures, typeName: typeName, instance: instance)
end 'buildServiceBehaviourPair'

// ⭐ **THE STATE'S TYPE IS WHERE THE WHOLE PER-INSTANCE ABI COMES FROM.** A `genericInstance`
// here is what makes `MaxonToStdLowering.materializeLayoutArgFor` hand each handler
// `__layout_<mangled>` and `managedFieldDropCallee` hand the finish `__destruct_<mangled>` — both
// read the state value's own type, so naming the instantiation once supplies every dictionary these
// bodies need. It is INDEX-SPACE, because the state value is MINTED (`SynthesizedFunction.mint` crosses
// the id into the project's table).
function serviceStateTypeOf(signatures ProgramSignatures, typeName ByteArray, instance ServiceStateInstance) returns MaxonType
	let indexNames = signatures.indexTypeNames()

	return match instance 'i'
		monomorphic gives MaxonType.structRef(indexNames.intern(typeName))
		at(id) gives MaxonType.genericInstance(id)
	end 'i'
end 'serviceStateTypeOf'

function loadServiceState(fn SynthesizedFunction, stateType MaxonType, site SynthesizedSite) returns ValueId
	let state = fn.mintOfType(stateType)
	fn.emit(MaxonOp.loadIndirect(state, addr: ServiceCownParam, offset: CownOffState, valueType: MaxonType.integer), site: site)
	return state
end 'loadServiceState'

// ⭐⭐ **`<T>.__behave(cown, request)` — ONE MESSAGE, and its shape is the answer to "what does a service DO?".**
//
// ```
// entry:     state = loadIndirect(cown, CownOffState)
//            switch loadIndirect(request, tag)
//              case k   -> load each payload, call <T>.<m>(state, …), drop what the
//                          handler did not consume, return
//              default  -> __cown_unknown_tag()  // aborts
// ```
function buildServiceBehave(module MaxonModule, project Project, signatures ProgramSignatures, funcNames FunctionNameIndex, typeName ByteArray, instance ServiceStateInstance)
	let stateType = serviceStateTypeOf(signatures, typeName: typeName, instance: instance)

	let paramTypes = MaxonTypeArray.create(0)
	paramTypes.push(MaxonType.integer)
	paramTypes.push(MaxonType.integer)
	let fn = SynthesizedFunction.open(module, project: project, name: serviceBehaveSymbolFor(signatures, typeName: typeName, instance: instance), returnType: MaxonReturnType.void, paramTypes: paramTypes)

	let site = SynthesizedSite.compilersOwn
	let request = requireServiceRequestLayout(signatures, typeName: typeName)

	let entry = fn.currentBlock()
	let state = loadServiceState(fn, stateType: stateType, site: site)
	let tag = fn.mintOfType(MaxonType.integer)
	fn.emit(MaxonOp.loadIndirect(tag, addr: ServiceRequestParam, offset: UnionTagOffset, valueType: MaxonType.integer), site: site)

	// The unknown-tag block is opened BEFORE the arms so the switch has its default block id, and the arms
	// are the switch's dense table in TAG order — `request.tagOfIndex(i)`
	// is `i` by construction (`ServiceCompanions.addServiceRequestCase` derives each tag from the
	// case count), so the table's index IS the case index.
	let unknownTag = buildUnknownTagBlock(fn, site: site)

	let armIds = BlockIdArray.create(request.caseCount(), zeroed: false)

	for caseIndex in 0 upto request.caseCount() 'eachVariant'
		armIds.push(buildMessageArm(fn, signatures: signatures, funcNames: funcNames, callee: qualifiedMethodName(typeName, methodName: request.caseNameAt(caseIndex)), instance: instance, request: request, caseIndex: caseIndex, state: state, site: site))
	end 'eachVariant'

	fn.terminateBlock(entry, op: MaxonOp.switch(tag, denseTargetBlockIds: armIds, defaultBlockId: unknownTag.id), site: site)
end 'buildServiceBehave'

// ⭐ **`<T>.__finish(cown)` — THE STATE'S ONE DROP.** The state was moved into the cown by the start
// behaviour's last store, and the runner calls this only while that store holds a state, then stores 0 back.
function buildServiceFinish(module MaxonModule, project Project, signatures ProgramSignatures, typeName ByteArray, instance ServiceStateInstance)
	let stateType = serviceStateTypeOf(signatures, typeName: typeName, instance: instance)

	let paramTypes = MaxonTypeArray.create(0)
	paramTypes.push(MaxonType.integer)
	let fn = SynthesizedFunction.open(module, project: project, name: serviceFinishSymbolFor(signatures, typeName: typeName, instance: instance), returnType: MaxonReturnType.void, paramTypes: paramTypes)

	let site = SynthesizedSite.compilersOwn
	let state = loadServiceState(fn, stateType: stateType, site: site)
	fn.emitPositionalCallDiscarding(managedFieldDropCallee(signatures, typeNames: signatures.indexTypeNames(), fieldType: stateType), args: argsOf(state), site: site)
	fn.terminate(MaxonOp.retVoid, site: site)
end 'buildServiceFinish'

function buildUnknownTagBlock(fn SynthesizedFunction, site SynthesizedSite) returns IrBlock
	let unknownTag = fn.openBlock(b"unknowntag")

	fn.emitPositionalCallDiscarding(CownUnknownTagName, args: ValueIdArray.create(0), site: site)
	fn.terminate(MaxonOp.retVoid, site: site)
	return unknownTag
end 'buildUnknownTagBlock'

function dropLoadedPayload(fn SynthesizedFunction, signatures ProgramSignatures, request EnumLayout, field PayloadField, class PayloadClass, loaded ValueId, site SynthesizedSite)
	if payloadClassIsExistential(class) 'aFatPointer'
		fn.emitPositionalCallDiscarding(DropExistentialName, args: twoArgs(fn.witnessOf(loaded), second: loaded), site: site)
		return
	end 'aFatPointer'

	fn.emitPositionalCallDiscarding(managedFieldDropCallee(signatures, typeNames: signatures.indexTypeNames(), fieldType: signatures.payloadTypeOf(field, layout: request, into: signatures.indexTypeNames())), args: argsOf(loaded), site: site)
end 'dropLoadedPayload'

function buildMessageArm(fn SynthesizedFunction, signatures ProgramSignatures, funcNames FunctionNameIndex, callee ByteArray, instance ServiceStateInstance, request EnumLayout, caseIndex CaseIndex, state ValueId, site SynthesizedSite) returns BlockId
	let armId = fn.openBlock(request.caseNameAt(caseIndex)).id
	let payloads = request.payloadsAt(caseIndex)

	// The declaration this variant was built from. Its `paramTypes` count is how many of the variant's
	// payloads are ARGUMENTS (the rest is the reply slot), which is what the payload loop below is bounded by; the
	// "it cannot miss" invariant is `ServiceCompanions.serviceDeclarationOf`'s, stated once for all the
	// places that rest on it.
	let decl = serviceDeclarationOf(signatures, key: callee)

	// ⚠ **ONLY THE DECLARED PARAMETERS ARE LOADED, AND THE `__reply` SLOT IS NOT ONE.** A message with a
	// reply carries its cell in a trailing slot; loading it would hand the handler an argument its declaration
	// does not have.
	let args = ValueIdArray.create(0)
	args.push(state)
	let payloadClasses = LoadedPayloadClassArray.create(decl.paramTypes.count(), zeroed: false)
	let payloadTypes = MaxonTypeArray.create(decl.paramTypes.count(), zeroed: false)

	for param in 0 upto decl.paramTypes.count() 'eachParam'
		let slot = serviceParamPayloadSlot(payloads, paramIndex: param as ParamCount)
		let field = try payloads.get(slot) otherwise panic("buildMessageArm: `serviceParamPayloadSlot` answered slot {slot} of a variant holding {payloads.count()} payload(s)")
		let declared = signatures.payloadTypeOf(field, layout: request, into: signatures.indexTypeNames())
		let class = classifyUnionPayload(signatures, typeNames: signatures.indexTypeNames(), fieldType: declared, slotScopeFilePath: request.declFilePath)
		payloadClasses.push(class)
		let valueType = payloadValueTypeOf(class, declared: declared)
		payloadTypes.push(valueType)
		args.push(loadPayloadWord(fn, box: ServiceRequestParam, offset: request.payloadSlotOffset(slot), class: class, valueType: valueType, site: site))
	end 'eachParam'

	// ⭐ **THE HANDLER'S RETURN TYPE IS DERIVED ONCE AND THREADED.** The call and the completion must agree
	// about a type this instantiation SUBSTITUTED, and two derivations of one substitution are two chances
	// to disagree about which register the reply's value word came back in.
	let returned = try serviceHandlerReturnType(signatures, callee: callee, instance: instance, typeNames: signatures.indexTypeNames()) otherwise panic("buildMessageArm: '{String.from(callee)}' has a declaration (`serviceDeclarationOf` just answered) yet records no return type — both read the one declaration sweep")
	let reply = serviceArmReply(fn, request: request, caseIndex: caseIndex, payloads: payloads, req: ServiceRequestParam, site: site)
	let cells = spillReassignedPayloads(fn, byReference: funcNames.byReferenceParamsOf(callee), classes: payloadClasses, types: payloadTypes, args: args, site: site)
	let outcome = emitServiceHandlerCall(fn, callee: callee, returned: returned, signatures: signatures, args: handlerArgsOf(args, cells: cells), site: site)
	reclaimReassignedPayloads(fn, cells: cells, args: args, site: site)

	// ⛔⛔⛔ **EVERY RELEASE THIS GREEN THREAD OWES HAPPENS BEFORE THE PUBLISH, AND THAT ORDER IS THE WHOLE
	// REASON THE CALL AND THE COMPLETION ARE TWO FUNCTIONS.** `__gt_cell_complete` stores `completed`, which is
	// the instant the AWAITER may resume — on another M. Anything `__behave` touches after that line it touches
	// while a second green thread is running, and a COUNTED box's reference count is a plain load/add/store
	// (`MmRuntime.emitAdjustRefcount`) precisely because one green thread at a time holds it; only a box a share walk
	// marked shared steps atomically.
	//
	// ⚠ **AND THE TWO REALLY CAN NAME ONE BOX.** A message may return a record with a managed FIELD, and a
	// handler may build that record over a message PARAMETER — `Wrapper.of(s)` co-owns `s`, so the string is
	// named by the reply the awaiter now holds AND by this message, whose reference
	// `dropUnconsumedPayloads` is about to give back. Published first, those two decrements are two green
	// threads stepping one count with no atomic between them: a race by construction, however narrow, and the
	// ordering that removes it costs nothing. It is the rule `GtRuntime.emitGtTeardownArrive` states for the
	// teardown word: **every read or release of shared state precedes the arrival that hands it over.**
	dropUnconsumedPayloads(fn, signatures: signatures, callee: callee, request: request, caseIndex: caseIndex, classes: payloadClasses, args: args, site: site)

	emitServiceReplyCompletion(fn, returned: returned, outcome: outcome, reply: reply, site: site)

	// ⛔⛔ **THE CURRENT BLOCK, NOT THE ARM'S ENTRY — THE TWO DIFFER FOR A THROWING HANDLER.** Its `tryCall`'s
	// error edge is a diamond (`emitServiceReplyCompletion`), so the ops above landed in that diamond's MERGE and
	// the entry is already terminated by its `condBranch`. Terminating the entry again would overwrite that
	// branch and skip the payload drops; `fn.terminate` closes wherever the ops ended up.
	fn.terminate(MaxonOp.retVoid, site: site)
	return armId
end 'buildMessageArm'

type ReassignedPayloadCell
	export let position as ParamCount
	export let cell as ValueId
	export let class as PayloadClass
	export let valueType as MaxonType

	static function create(position ParamCount, cell ValueId, class PayloadClass, valueType MaxonType) returns Self
		return Self{position: position, cell: cell, class: class, valueType: valueType}
	end 'create'
end 'ReassignedPayloadCell'

typealias ReassignedPayloadCellArray = Array with ReassignedPayloadCell

typealias LoadedPayloadClassArray = Array with PayloadClass

// A payload whose handler parameter is passed by reference is handed in a parameter cell, and
// `reclaimReassignedPayloads` reads the cell's final value back into `args` before
// `dropUnconsumedPayloads` runs: the handler may have replaced the value, and the drop must release
// what the cell holds, not what the message carried.
function spillReassignedPayloads(fn SynthesizedFunction, byReference ParamPositionMask, classes LoadedPayloadClassArray, types MaxonTypeArray, args ValueIdArray, site SynthesizedSite) returns ReassignedPayloadCellArray
	let cells = ReassignedPayloadCellArray.create(0)

	if byReference == NoParamPositions 'everyParameterByValue'
		return cells
	end 'everyParameterByValue'

	for param in 0 upto classes.count() 'eachPayload'
		let position = (param + ServiceReceiverArgCount) as ParamCount

		let valueType = try types.get(param) otherwise panic("spillReassignedPayloads: types.get OOB at {param} — one type is pushed per loaded parameter")

		if not parameterRidesACellIntoASpawn(byReference, param: position, paramType: valueType) 'passedByValue'
			continue
		end 'passedByValue'

		let class = try classes.get(param) otherwise panic("spillReassignedPayloads: classes.get OOB at {param} — one class is pushed per loaded parameter")
		let loaded = try args.get(position) otherwise panic("spillReassignedPayloads: args.get OOB at {position} — `args` holds the receiver followed by one value per parameter")
		let cell = fn.emitPositionalCall(ParameterCellAllocName, args: ValueIdArray.create(0), resultTag: maxonTypeTag(valueType), resultNameId: typeNameIdOf(valueType), site: site)
		fn.emit(MaxonOp.storeIndirect(cell, offset: ParameterCellValueOffset, value: loaded, valueType: payloadStorageOf(class)), site: site)

		if parameterCellHoldsAWitness(valueType) 'andItsWitnessHalf'
			fn.emit(MaxonOp.storeIndirect(cell, offset: ParameterCellWitnessOffset, value: fn.witnessOf(loaded), valueType: MaxonType.integer), site: site)
		end 'andItsWitnessHalf'

		cells.push(ReassignedPayloadCell.create(position, cell: cell, class: class, valueType: valueType))
	end 'eachPayload'

	return cells
end 'spillReassignedPayloads'

function handlerArgsOf(args ValueIdArray, cells ReassignedPayloadCellArray) returns ValueIdArray
	if cells.isEmpty() 'nothingSpilled'
		return args
	end 'nothingSpilled'

	let handed = ValueIdArray.create(0)
	handed.append(args)

	for spilled in cells 'eachCell'
		try handed.set(spilled.position, value: spilled.cell) otherwise panic("handlerArgsOf: handed.set OOB at {spilled.position}")
	end 'eachCell'

	return handed
end 'handlerArgsOf'

function reclaimReassignedPayloads(fn SynthesizedFunction, cells ReassignedPayloadCellArray, args ValueIdArray, site SynthesizedSite)
	for spilled in cells 'eachCell'
		let final = loadPayloadWord(fn, box: spilled.cell, offset: ParameterCellValueOffset, class: spilled.class, valueType: spilled.valueType, site: site)
		try args.set(spilled.position, value: final) otherwise panic("reclaimReassignedPayloads: args.set OOB at {spilled.position}")
		fn.emitPositionalCallDiscarding(MmDecrefName, args: argsOf(spilled.cell), site: site)
	end 'eachCell'
end 'reclaimReassignedPayloads'

function loadPayloadWord(fn SynthesizedFunction, box ValueId, offset ByteOffset, class PayloadClass, valueType MaxonType, site SynthesizedSite) returns ValueId
	let loaded = fn.mintOfType(valueType)
	fn.emit(MaxonOp.loadIndirect(loaded, addr: box, offset: offset, valueType: payloadStorageOf(class)), site: site)

	if payloadClassIsExistential(class) 'andItsWitnessHalf'
		let witness = fn.mintOfType(MaxonType.integer)
		fn.emit(MaxonOp.loadIndirect(witness, addr: box, offset: offset + InterfaceWitnessHalfOffset, valueType: MaxonType.integer), site: site)
		fn.pairWitness(loaded, witness: witness)
	end 'andItsWitnessHalf'

	return loaded
end 'loadPayloadWord'

// ⭐ **WHERE THIS ARM'S REPLY GOES, OR THAT IT HAS NONE.** `serviceReplySlotIndex` is the one
// authority on which variants carry a cell; this loads it where there is one.
function serviceArmReply(fn SynthesizedFunction, request EnumLayout, caseIndex CaseIndex, payloads PayloadFieldArray, req ValueId, site SynthesizedSite) returns ServiceReplyTarget
	match serviceReplySlotIndex(payloads) 'reply'
		absent then return ServiceReplyTarget.fireAndForget
		at then return ServiceReplyTarget.cell(loadServiceReplyCell(fn, request: request, caseIndex: caseIndex, payloads: payloads, req: req, site: site))
	end 'reply'
end 'serviceArmReply'

// The cell pointer out of this variant's `__reply` payload slot. Asked only where the slot exists, so the
// panic names a caller that skipped its own gate.
function loadServiceReplyCell(fn SynthesizedFunction, request EnumLayout, caseIndex CaseIndex, payloads PayloadFieldArray, req ValueId, site SynthesizedSite) returns ValueId
	let slot = match serviceReplySlotIndex(payloads) 'reply'
		absent panic("loadServiceReplyCell: variant `{String.from(request.caseNameAt(caseIndex))}` of `{String.from(request.name)}` carries no `__reply` payload — every caller gates on `serviceReplySlotIndex`")
		at(index) gives index
	end 'reply'

	let cell = fn.mintOfType(MaxonType.integer)
	fn.emit(MaxonOp.loadIndirect(cell, addr: req, offset: request.payloadSlotOffset(slot), valueType: MaxonType.integer), site: site)
	return cell
end 'loadServiceReplyCell'

// ⭐ **WHAT AN ARM OWES ITS SENDER.** A union rather than a `ValueId` plus a flag, for `ServiceReplyValue`'s
// reason one tier up: a fire-and-forget message has no cell at all, and `v0` is a real SSA value.
union ServiceReplyTarget
	fireAndForget
	cell(value ValueId)
end 'ServiceReplyTarget'

// ⭐⭐ **WHAT THE HANDLER PRODUCED, BEFORE ANY OF IT IS PUBLISHED.** The two shapes a message can have,
// carried from the call to the completion across the releases that must sit between them — see
// `buildMessageArm` for why that gap exists and what closing it would cost.
union ServiceHandlerOutcome
	// A non-throwing handler: one result register, which is `void` for a message that returns nothing.
	answered(result ValueId)

	// A throwing handler: the result register and the error flag its `tryCall` set.
	routed(result ValueId, errorFlag ValueId)
end 'ServiceHandlerOutcome'

// ⭐⭐ **THE HANDLER CALL, AND WHAT BECOMES OF ITS TWO OUTCOMES.** A message with a reply hands both
// to the CELL and drops neither: the awaiter takes the value's reference (`__gt_try_await` releases the
// arguments with the result CONSUMED) and reads the error word. A message WITHOUT a reply returns nothing
// and throws nothing by construction — that is exactly what `serviceMessageHasAReply` answers `false` for —
// so its call has no outcome to place at all.
//
// ⛔⛔ **SO THIS FILE DROPS NO RESULT AND NO ERROR.** Every value-returning or throwing message has a
// cell, and a thrown BOX cannot arrive: a message throwing a payload-carrying union is refused at
// the `spawn`, E3140, because a reply's one error word holds an ordinal and not a pointer. A
// drop of either would be unreachable, and an unreachable drop in a leak-gated compiler is a claim
// nothing can check.
//
// ⛔ **A `tryCall` OPENS AN ERROR-EDGE DIAMOND, so the ops after this call land in that diamond's MERGE
// rather than in the arm's own block** — see the terminator at the end of `buildMessageArm` for why it is
// `fn.terminate`.
//
// A plain `call` to a throwing callee is **E3057** at `SemanticCheck.validatePlainCall` (which walks this
// synthesized body like any other), so the `tryCall` is FORCED.
function emitServiceHandlerCall(fn SynthesizedFunction, callee ByteArray, returned MaxonReturnType, signatures ProgramSignatures, args ValueIdArray, site SynthesizedSite) returns ServiceHandlerOutcome
	let resultTag = match returned 'r'
		void gives ValueTypeTag.void
		value(inner) gives maxonTypeTag(inner)
	end 'r'

	let resultNameId = match returned 'n'
		void gives UnnamedTypeId
		value(inner) gives typeNameIdOf(inner)
	end 'n'

	if not throwsClauseIsThrowing(signatures.throwsOf(callee)) 'nonThrowing'
		let answered = fn.emitPositionalCall(callee, args: args, resultTag: resultTag, resultNameId: resultNameId, site: site)

		// A handler returning an interface-typed value hands its witness half back in the secondary return
		// register, which the lowering captures into the paired value (`LowerMaxonToStd.appendDirectCall`). Such
		// a declaration cannot also throw, so only this edge mints one.
		if resultTag == ValueTypeTag.interfaceRef 'aFatPointer'
			fn.pairWitness(answered, witness: fn.mintOfType(MaxonType.integer))
		end 'aFatPointer'

		return ServiceHandlerOutcome.answered(answered)
	end 'nonThrowing'

	let result = fn.mint(resultTag, nameId: resultNameId)
	let errorFlag = fn.mintOfType(MaxonType.integer)
	fn.emit(MaxonOp.tryCall(result, errorFlag: errorFlag, callee: callee, args: args, argLabels: emptyArgLabels(args), argRanges: uniformArgRanges(args, range: site.range()), argImmutableNames: NameRoster.create(0), mint: CalleeMint.notMinted), site: site)
	return ServiceHandlerOutcome.routed(result, errorFlag: errorFlag)
end 'emitServiceHandlerCall'

// ⭐⭐⭐ **PUBLISH THE ANSWER — THE LAST THING THIS ARM DOES TO A STRUCTURE ANYBODY ELSE CAN SEE.**
// `__gt_cell_complete` publishes `completed`, which is the instant the awaiter may resume on another M;
// `buildMessageArm` states what that costs when a release comes after it, and why every one of them is
// emitted above this call.
function emitServiceReplyCompletion(fn SynthesizedFunction, returned MaxonReturnType, outcome ServiceHandlerOutcome, reply ServiceReplyTarget, site SynthesizedSite)
	match outcome 'o'
		answered(result) then publishAnsweredReply(fn, returned: returned, result: result, reply: reply, site: site)
		routed(result, errorFlag) then emitRoutedReplyCompletion(fn, returned: returned, result: result, errorFlag: errorFlag, reply: reply, site: site)
	end 'o'
end 'emitServiceReplyCompletion'

// The THROWING handler's two edges. Split from the arm above because a `match` arm is one statement and this
// is a diamond.
function emitRoutedReplyCompletion(fn SynthesizedFunction, returned MaxonReturnType, result ValueId, errorFlag ValueId, reply ServiceReplyTarget, site SynthesizedSite)
	let threw = fn.emitCompare(errorFlag, rhs: fn.emitTypedLiteral(NoErrorFlag, valueType: MaxonType.integer, site: site), op: MaxonCmpOp.ne, site: site)
	let caught = fn.currentBlock()

	let thrown = fn.openBlock(b"replythrew")
	completeServiceReply(fn, reply: reply, result: fn.emitTypedLiteral(0, valueType: MaxonType.integer, site: site), threw: errorFlag, site: site)

	// ⚠ On the THROWN path the success register holds whatever the exit left there — the undefined slot
	// `AsyncReleaser`'s header calls a wild free — so the VALUE word is written only on the edge that really
	// produced one, and the thrown edge writes a 0 the releaser's null guard reads as "nothing was put here".
	let answered = fn.openBlock(b"replyok")
	publishAnsweredReply(fn, returned: returned, result: result, reply: reply, site: site)

	let handled = fn.openBlock(b"handled")
	fn.terminateBlock(caught, op: MaxonOp.condBranch(threw, thenBlockId: thrown.id, elseBlockId: answered.id), site: site)
	fn.terminateBlock(thrown, op: MaxonOp.branch(handled.id), site: site)
	fn.terminateBlock(answered, op: MaxonOp.branch(handled.id), site: site)
	fn.resumeBlock(handled)
end 'emitRoutedReplyCompletion'

// One reply answered, or nothing at all for a fire-and-forget message. Written once because both edges of a
// throwing call and the whole of a non-throwing one reach it, and the ORDER of the three words
// `__gt_cell_complete` writes is the runtime's to state, not this file's.
function completeServiceReply(fn SynthesizedFunction, reply ServiceReplyTarget, result ValueId, threw ValueId, site SynthesizedSite)
	match reply 'r'
		fireAndForget then return
		cell(value) then fn.emitPositionalCallDiscarding(GtCellCompleteName, args: threeArgs(value, second: result, third: threw), site: site)
	end 'r'
end 'completeServiceReply'

// The edge on which the handler really produced its value: the completion. A void call names no value at all,
// so its word is a literal 0 — "there is nothing here" in a word that must always be written.
function publishAnsweredReply(fn SynthesizedFunction, returned MaxonReturnType, result ValueId, reply ServiceReplyTarget, site SynthesizedSite)
	let threw = fn.emitTypedLiteral(NoErrorFlag, valueType: MaxonType.integer, site: site)

	match returned 'r'
		void then completeServiceReply(fn, reply: reply, result: fn.emitTypedLiteral(0, valueType: MaxonType.integer, site: site), threw: threw, site: site)
		value(replyType) then publishReplyValue(fn, replyType: replyType, result: result, reply: reply, threw: threw, site: site)
	end 'r'
end 'publishAnsweredReply'

function publishReplyValue(fn SynthesizedFunction, replyType MaxonType, result ValueId, reply ServiceReplyTarget, threw ValueId, site SynthesizedSite)
	if maxonTypeTag(replyType) == ValueTypeTag.interfaceRef 'aFatPointer'
		storeReplyWitness(fn, reply: reply, witness: fn.witnessOf(result), site: site)
	end 'aFatPointer'

	completeServiceReply(fn, reply: reply, result: result, threw: threw, site: site)
end 'publishReplyValue'

// ⭐ **A REPLY HELD AT AN INTERFACE TYPE CARRIES ITS WITNESS HALF IN A THIRD WORD OF THE CELL**
// (`GtRuntime.GtOffReplyWitness`), written before `__gt_cell_complete` publishes the other two because the
// awaiter reads it once `completed` is visible (`GtRuntime.GtReplyWitnessName`).
function storeReplyWitness(fn SynthesizedFunction, reply ServiceReplyTarget, witness ValueId, site SynthesizedSite)
	match reply 'r'
		fireAndForget then panic("storeReplyWitness: a message returning a value has no reply cell — `serviceMessageHasAReply` gives every value-returning message one")
		cell(value) then fn.emit(MaxonOp.storeIndirect(value, offset: GtOffReplyWitness, value: witness, valueType: MaxonType.integer), site: site)
	end 'r'
end 'storeReplyWitness'

// ⭐⭐ **DROP EVERY MANAGED PAYLOAD THE HANDLER DID NOT TAKE OWNERSHIP OF.** The message holds
// exactly one reference to each of its managed payloads — the one the send moved in — and the
// handler either consumed it or borrowed it. A borrowed one is still `__behave`'s to release,
// through the ordinary drop, and releasing it is what balances the move.
//
// ⚠ **`consumeOf(callee).isConsumedAt` ANSWERS `false` FOR EVERY MESSAGE, AND THAT IS A CHECKED
// ANSWER, NOT A SKIP.** The sweep reads every declaration's parameters, an instance method's
// included, but only three doors can mark one consumed and a message handler can hold none of them:
// a direct `Self{f: p}` store in an instance method is co-ownership rather than a move
// (`Parser.scanBodyFacts`, `detectFieldStores: false`); a type-parameter feed needs a payload typed
// at one, and a promise reclaim needs a `Promise` payload — and `untransferableParameterNoun`
// refuses BOTH at the `spawn` (E3217), reading the handler's declared slot type: a send cannot know
// an opaque `T`'s layout, and a promise owns a green thread its awaiter holds. Asking the ONE door
// rather than hard-coding that costs a map lookup per payload at compile time and is what keeps
// this correct the day a fourth door opens; hard-coding it would be a double free that day.
//
// ⚠ The index is CALL-ALIGNED — the receiver is position 0 — which is the space `ParamConsumeInfo`'s columns
// are recorded in (`Parser.recordScannedSignature` states it), and `args` is built in that same order.
function dropUnconsumedPayloads(fn SynthesizedFunction, signatures ProgramSignatures, callee ByteArray, request EnumLayout, caseIndex CaseIndex, classes LoadedPayloadClassArray, args ValueIdArray, site SynthesizedSite)
	let payloads = request.payloadsAt(caseIndex)

	for param in 0 upto classes.count() 'eachPayload'
		let class = try classes.get(param) otherwise panic("dropUnconsumedPayloads: classes.get OOB at {param} — one class is pushed per loaded parameter")

		if not payloadClassIsManaged(class) 'ownsNoHeap'
			continue
		end 'ownsNoHeap'

		if signatures.consumeOf(callee).isConsumedAt((param + ServiceReceiverArgCount) as ParamCount) 'theHandlerTookIt'
			continue
		end 'theHandlerTookIt'

		let loaded = try args.get(param + ServiceReceiverArgCount) otherwise panic("dropUnconsumedPayloads: args.get OOB at {param + ServiceReceiverArgCount} — `args` holds the receiver followed by one value per parameter")

		let field = try payloads.get(serviceParamPayloadSlot(payloads, paramIndex: param as ParamCount)) otherwise panic("dropUnconsumedPayloads: `serviceParamPayloadSlot` answered a slot past the variant's payloads")
		dropLoadedPayload(fn, signatures: signatures, request: request, field: field, class: class, loaded: loaded, site: site)
	end 'eachPayload'
end 'dropUnconsumedPayloads'

// `args[0]` of a message dispatch is the service's own state — the receiver, which fills no payload slot. So
// payload `j` is `args[j + ServiceReceiverArgCount]`, exactly as `MaxonDialect.WitnessReceiverArgCount`
// states the same kind of fact for a witness dispatch.
let ServiceReceiverArgCount = 1 as ParamCount

// A handler's return type AS THE INSTANTIATION THIS PAIR SERVES FIXES IT. The substitution is what gives a
// `returns T` handler's result the same concrete tag the awaiter reads it back at; the reply cell's
// own type was substituted through the same instance at the send
// (`SignatureIndex.internPromiseInstanceForReply`).
function serviceHandlerReturnType(signatures ProgramSignatures, callee ByteArray, instance ServiceStateInstance, typeNames TypeNameInterner) returns MaxonReturnType throws AbsentError
	let declaredReturn = try signatures.declaredReturnTypeOf(callee, into: typeNames)
	return serviceInstanceResolvedReturn(signatures, returnType: declaredReturn, declFilePath: signatures.recordedReturnDeclFileOf(callee), instance: instance)
end 'serviceHandlerReturnType'
